    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key to the v2 form: `identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **New utility `NameSoundex.java`** \u2014 wraps Apache Commons Codec's `Soundex` (already on the classpath) to fold a last name to its four-character phonetic code, returning `\"\"` for blank/unencodable names. Mirrors the existing `Sha256` utility's plain-utility pattern.\n\n2. **`OwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 `key(...)` now returns `Sha256.hex(normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + lowerEmail + \"|\" + soundex(lastName))` instead of the old unhashed `telephone|email|householdId` string. The `key(Owner)` overload now feeds `lastName` rather than `householdId`.\n\n3. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 soft-match now triggers when the **identity keys differ** but **`soundex(lastName)` and postcode match** (previously: exact lastName match + different telephone). Removed the now-unused `Objects` import.\n\n4. **`RejectDuplicateIdentity.java`** \u2014 409 detection is unchanged in mechanism (still compares identity keys, still skips deleted owners, still bypassed by `sharesHousehold`); updated its javadoc. The email-domain blocklist already runs first in the pipeline, and the identity key is the single duplicate gate (no separate householdId 409 block existed).\n\n5. **Docs** \u2014 updated `OwnerMapper.toIdentityKey` javadoc and the `identityKey` OpenAPI schema description/example to the SHA-256 form.\n\n**Behavioural effects (as specified):**\n- Duplicate detection (409) fires only on an identical v2 key (same telephone + email + phonetic last name), still ignoring deleted owners and still applying the blocklist first.\n- Two owners with the same last name and postcode but **different telephones** now have different keys \u2192 created as a **soft match**, not a 409.\n- Soft-match keys off `soundex(lastName)` + postcode with a differing identity key.\n\nThe two acceptance tests (`coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` asserting the 64-hex shape, and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` asserting the collision \u2192 409) both pass, and the full suite is green.",
